# Security Rules

Treat progress photos as sensitive private user data. Workout data and photos are private by default.

Never:

- log passwords
- log authentication tokens
- log private photo URLs
- expose database errors directly to users
- put secrets in source code
- disable RLS
- create public access to progress photos
- hardcode Supabase service-role keys
- put secret API keys in the mobile application
- trust client-provided user IDs
- store authentication tokens manually unless required by the SDK

Validate all user input. Use Zod for client-side validation where appropriate. Server/database constraints remain authoritative.

`.env` must not be committed. `.env.example` may list `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` only.
